# Where the match API answers while developing. Committed on purpose: it is a localhost port, not a
# secret, and every developer wants the same one.
#
# This WINS over the dev proxy in vite.config.ts, and the two exist for different situations: the proxy
# needs nothing configured and keeps the client same-origin, while this points straight at the Worker —
# which is what production does (the site is on pages.dev and the API on workers.dev), so developing
# against it is developing against the real shape. Cross-origin means the Worker's CORS is exercised
# here rather than discovered on the first deploy.
#
# Change the port if `wrangler dev` picked another one; it does when 8787 is already taken.
VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787
